<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>JQuery Example</title>
    <style>
        .feedback {
            display: none;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>JQUERY EXAMPLE</h1>

    <h2 id="toggle1">=> Space Exploration</h2>

    <p id="first">Space exploration represents humanity's innate drive to discover the unknown and expand our cosmic horizons.
    <br>Venturing beyond Earth not only satisfies our boundless curiosity but also drives incredible technological innovation.
    <br>From developing water filtration systems to improving satellite communications, the offshoots of these missions heavily benefit daily life.
    <br>Moreover, establishing a multi-planetary presence acts as an insurance policy for the long-term survival of our species.
    <br>As we push forward to the Moon, Mars, and beyond, we edge closer to unlocking the deepest secrets of the universe.
    </p>
    <button id="hide1">Hide this text</button>
    <button id="show1">Show the hidden text</button>

    <p></p>
     
    <h2 id="toggle2">=> Northern Lights</h2>

    <p id="second">The Aurora Borealis, or Northern Lights, is a dazzling natural light display primarily seen in high-latitude regions.
    <br>It occurs when charged particles from the sun collide with Earth's magnetic field and atmospheric gases. 
    <br>This collision creates vibrant, dancing ribbons of green, pink, and violet light across the night sky. 
    <br>The most intense and frequent displays typically happen around the magnetic poles during the winter months. 
    <br>For stargazers in the Northern Hemisphere, clear, dark skies provide the best conditions to witness this spectacular astronomical event.
    </p>
    <button id="hide2">Hide this text</button>
    <button id="show2">Show the hidden text</button>

    <br><br><br>
    
    <button id="toggle3">GIVE YOUR FEEDBACK</button>
    <div class="feedback" id="feedback">
    <h3>=> How did you find the information?<h3>
    <button id="yes">IT WAS GOOD</button>
    <button id="no">COULD BE BETTER</button>
    </div>
    
    <script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-4.0.0.js" integrity="sha256-9fsHeVnKBvqh3FB2HYu7g2xseAZ5MlN6Kz/qnkASV8U=" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
    <script>
    $("#yes").click(function(){
        alert('Thankyou very much for giving your time and reading this!');
    })

    $("#no").click(function(){
        alert('We will try to make it better.. thanks for your feedback!');
    })
     
    $("#hide1").click(function(){
      $("#first").hide(speed="slow");
    });

    $("#show1").click(function(){
      $("#first").show(speed="slow");
    });

    $("#toggle1").click(function(){
      $("#first").toggle(speed="slow");
    });

    $("#hide2").click(function(){
      $("#second").hide(speed="slow");
    });

    $("#show2").click(function(){
      $("#second").show(speed="slow");
    });

    $("#toggle2").click(function(){
      $("#second").toggle(speed="slow");
    });

    $("#toggle3").click(function(){
      $("#feedback").toggle(speed="slow");
    });

    </script>
</body>
</html>
